        "content": "Goal: import the character sheet a user provides into the SealDice character card of the current group/private-chat context. Prefer the complete .st import command already generated by the sheet; never reorder or guess attributes.\n\n1. Read the file\n1. Get the real path or URL from the file fields of the current message (prefer path/file/url, then file_id). If only a file name is available without an accessible path, clearly ask the user to resend the file or provide a path; never guess a local location.\n2. For .xlsx/.xlsm files, use mcp-files-exec read_file or run_shell with Python/openpyxl/LibreOffice. List the worksheets first and prefer the one named \"简化卡 骰娘导入\" (or one containing \"简化卡\" / \"骰娘导入\"), then fall back to Sheet2/the second worksheet. The templates under D:COC空白卡 are only for recognizing the layout and must not replace the sheet the user actually uploaded.\n3. When reading formula results, prefer the cached calculated value; if the cache is empty, recalculate headlessly with LibreOffice first. Never treat formula text itself as .st arguments.\n\n2. Extract .st\n1. Scan all cells of the preferred worksheet (including formula results and rich/line-wrapped text) for a complete command starting with .st. Leading/trailing whitespace and full-width spaces are allowed, but keep the field order, equals signs, plus/minus signs, parentheses and separators of the original command.\n2. Prefer the complete character-card import command (containing the character name and multiple attributes) and exclude query, cleanup or partial-edit commands such as \".st show/.st clr/.st rm\". If the sheet produces multiple .st lines, run them in sheet order; before running, show the user a summary of the commands and confirm the character name to avoid overwriting the wrong character.\n3. Import with the core tool run_core_command, not run_ext_command:\n   {\"action\":\"call\",\"raw_message\":\".st …\",\"forward\":true}\n   raw_message cannot be combined with command/args. When omitted, forward already defaults to true; pass false explicitly only if the user asks for silence.\n4. After the command returns, confirm with a core st query through run_core_command (usually {\"action\":\"call\",\"command\":\"st\",\"args\":[\"show\"]}) and check the character name and key attributes. On failure do not blindly retry; report the core response first.\n\n3. Fallback when no usable .st exists\n1. Confirm the character name first, then use core character management: {\"action\":\"call\",\"command\":\"pc\",\"args\":[\"new\",\"<character name>\"],\"forward\":true}. If the character already exists, do not overwrite it; query with pc list/st show and ask for confirmation first.\n2. After creating it, set the recognizable attributes from the sheet in batches with core st syntax, still via run_core_command(command=\"st\", args=[…]). List unknown fields, unresolved formulas or unmappable fields as needing manual handling; never guess values.\n3. Run st show once more to verify. When replying, report: file, worksheet, whether a direct .st was found, character name, execution result and fields not imported."
